    "duo_cos_alpha": {
      "params": [
        "node"
      ],
      "description": "cos(alpha) per cell, shaped [tile, x_metric, y_metric], where alpha is the angle between the two local curvilinear coordinate directions (Chen 2021 C17). This single scalar IS the entire metric on this grid: g_ij = [[1, cos a],[cos a, 1]], g^ij = (1/sin^2 a)[[1,-cos a],[-cos a,1]], sqrt(g)=sin(alpha) (C18-C20). Built as the C13-C14 TANGENT directions e1 ~ (k x k_i+1) x k, e2 ~ (k x k_j+1) x k via duo_tangent_cos. SOURCED FROM NODES: k(i,j) is taken as the RAW SUM of the four corner nodes of cell (i,j) (an unnormalised cell-centre direction); duo_tangent_cos is scale-invariant in each of its three point arguments, so the omitted 1/4 and the omitted renormalisation onto the sphere both cancel and the cos(alpha) is identical (to machine precision) to the duo_cell_center-based form. Sourcing from `node` rather than `center` lets the metric span x_metric = N+6 (interior + 3 ghost layers) using the node halo x_nodes_ext = N+8, one layer wider than the collocated cell-centre array x_cell_ext = N+6 -- which the 5-point (Ng=3) flux reconstruction requires at the outermost ghost cell, where a centre-based metric would need a non-existent forward centre. cos(alpha) is 0 at a tile centre and about -+0.45 at the cube corners. Bind `node` to duo_node_cart.",
      "body": {
        "op": "aggregate",
        "output_idx": [
          "gt",
          "gi",
          "gj"
        ],
        "args": [
          "node"
        ],
        "ranges": {
          "gt": {
            "from": "tile"
          },
          "gi": {
            "from": "x_metric"
          },
          "gj": {
            "from": "y_metric"
          }
        },
        "expr": {
          "op": "apply_expression_template",
          "args": [],
          "name": "duo_tangent_cos",
          "bindings": {
            "kax": {
              "op": "+",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "node",
                    "gt",
                    "gi",
                    "gj",
                    1
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
                    "node",
                    "gt",
                    {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        "gi",
                        1
                      ]
                    },
                    "gj",
                    1
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "op": "index",
                  "args": [
